{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Widened file_impact to declare src/rebar/mcp_server.py. The merged commit 44448546db6fd851e70049a2f68dd726ebac64ed carries the only `rebar-ticket: 326f-595a-088b-40a5` trailer on origin/main; all 14 of its changed paths are now declared. mcp_server.py re-exports FsckOut (import block + __all__) so the new model is reachable through the same import path every peer _Out model uses - a deliberate part of the fix, raised by the code review's critical advisory, not incidental churn. Live-validated against deployed container rebar-mcp-6fe5c0d54574-8093: the MCP fsck tool now returns a structured result with keys issues/fixed/issue_count/returncode/mode/report (issue_count=14, mode=scan) and no command_failed envelope."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787890289847762001,"uuid":"24521cd5-7012-407c-87b5-d68407acaba8"}